From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:52:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: record reviewed block relay hash conversion rules

Track eleven exact block/header relay and block-read-error call mappings. BlockHash is the actual referenced uint256, and Height/PeerId retain actual source integers. Keep optional hash versus end/none sentinel cases unchanged. Preserve all original branches, severity, category and human text, including leading spaces. Anticipated artifact source passes exact AST/idempotence and actual-flag syntax checks; no applied daemon behavior or functional-suite claim in this rule-data commit.

Coordinator integration provenance (canonical283 to ordered301):
The scripted commands, tool/rule hashes and historical validation receipts above are original-author provenance for the authored parent. They were not rerun on this composed parent and do not claim byte-for-byte regeneration or validation of it.
Application: git am -3 --keep-cr --keep-non-patch of the exact sealed original mailbox; no new conversion rollout.
Original mailbox applied without source-semantic adaptation at the shared insertion boundary; later explicit native removals are preserved separately.
Composed compile/runtime: pending; no suites or benchmarks run during integration.
